---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout title="How to Use EverywhereJob | EverywhereJob" description="Follow these steps to compare countries and plan your move.">
  <style>
    .card { background: #18181b; border-radius: 6px; padding: 2.5rem; border: 1px solid #27272a; margin-top: 2rem; }
    h1 { font-size: 2.25rem; color: #ffffff; font-weight: 800; letter-spacing: -0.03em; margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 1rem; text-transform: uppercase; }
    .subtitle { font-size: 1.05rem; color: #a1a1aa; margin-bottom: 3rem; }
    
    .guide-step { margin-bottom: 2.5rem; border-bottom: 1px solid #27272a; padding-bottom: 2.5rem; }
    .guide-step:last-child { border-bottom: none; padding-bottom: 0; margin-bottom: 0; }
    .step-title { color: #10b981; font-size: 1.25rem; font-weight: 700; margin-bottom: 1rem; }
    p { color: #e4e4e7; line-height: 1.6; margin: 0; }
  </style>

  <div class="wrapper">
    <div class="card">
      <h1>How to Use EverywhereJob</h1>
      <p class="subtitle">Follow these steps to compare countries and plan your move.</p>
      
      <div class="guide-step">
        <h2 class="step-title">Step 1: Find Your Role or Destination</h2>
        <p>Search for your current job title or the country you want to move to to see average salaries and costs.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="guide-step">
        <h2 class="step-title">Step 2: Check Visa Requirements</h2>
        <p>Review the specific routes available for your profession, whether you are looking for local employment or a remote digital nomad visa.</p>
      </div>
      
      <div class="guide-step">
        <h2 class="step-title">Step 3: Compare Markets</h2>
        <p>Use our Market Comparison Engine to evaluate local compensation, living costs, and net surplus between two target countries simultaneously.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</Layout>